    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Hurricane Maria\r\n\r\n::: details [**✅ Step 1**]\r\n**Evaluate the Dataset:**\r\n- Run the code to see information and statistics about the dataset.\r\n- Use `min()` , `max()` and `sum()` to identify the minimum, maximum and total sea surface temperatures.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**✅ Step 2**]\r\n**Summarize the Data:**\r\n- Use the `agg()` function to calculate the total, average, minimum, and maximum sea surface temperatures for each date.\r\n- Use `groupby()` if applicable to summarize the data over time. \r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**✅ Step 3**]\r\n**Interpret the Data:**\r\nDiscuss with a partner what the calculated statistics reveal about the sea surface temperatures during Hurricane Maria. Are there any significant trends or anomalies?\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**✅ Step 4**]\r\n**Form a Hypothesis:**\r\nDiscuss with a partner and create a brief hypothesis about the data. Consider what factors or broader events might be influencing the data and the trends, patterns or anomalies you identified.\r\n:::\r\n",
